All 15 tests pass. Here's what was fixed across the three modules:

**`src/auth.py`**:
- `has_permission`: Added case-insensitive comparison by lowercasing both the required role and each user role (`auth.py:9`).
- `is_admin_or_owner`: Changed `and` to `or` so either admin status or owner match grants access (`auth.py:15`).

**`src/inventory.py`**:
- `__init__`: Replaced the mutable default argument `{}` with `None` and copied any passed dict, preventing shared state across instances (`inventory.py:12`).
- `add`: Changed from replacing stock to accumulating it (`self._stock[sku] = self._stock.get(sku, 0) + qty`) (`inventory.py:17`).
- `reserve`: Changed `>=` to `>` so reserving exactly the available amount is allowed (`inventory.py:25`).
- `release`: Added a guard raising `ValueError` when releasing more than was reserved (`inventory.py:33`).

**`src/text_utils.py`**:
- `slugify`: Lowercased characters during iteration and replaced the single `--` → `-` replacement with a loop that collapses all repeated separators (`text_utils.py:15-19`).
- `truncate`: Shortened the slice by `len(suffix)` so the total output length (including suffix) respects `max_len` (`text_utils.py:30`).
